        "subject": "LU-21194 tests: use server page size in sanity 150f, 151, 156",
        "message": "LU-21194 tests: use server page size in sanity 150f, 151, 156\n\nsanity 151 and 156 (via roc_hit_init) write the file with bs=4k and\nexpect the OSS cache_access/cache_hit counters to rise by one per 4k\npage.  The OSD counts one per OSS page, so with 64KiB OSS pages a 16KiB\nread raises the counter by 1 instead of 4 and the tests fail with\n\"roc_hit is not safe to use\".  Write whole OSS pages, using\nget_page_size ost1, so that the expected counter change is the same\nfor any OSS page size.\n\nsanity 150f expects a 20KiB file to use 40 sectors and 24 after\npunching 8KiB.  The OSD maps and writes whole pages, so with 64KiB\nserver pages the last page is fully allocated: the file uses 128\nsectors, 112 after the punch, and the test fails with \"punch failed:\nblocks 112 != 24\".  Add the unused part of the last server page to the\nexpected counts, using the page size of ost1, or of mds1 with DOM.\nAlso keep the second sub-case (a 3000 byte punch, which frees no whole\nblock) at the full allocation.\n\nThe client page size does not matter here: $PAGE_SIZE is the client's\nand must not be used for these server-side counts.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: clientarch=aarch64 clientdistro=rocky9.8 testlist=sanity\nSigned-off-by: Di Wang <diwa@nvidia.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I3f3fbd6cd967f5962d58d7bc7644fe020f1f05d7\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
